# Prettier is configured with `endOfLine: "lf"`, which checks the bytes on disk.
#
# Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) checks every file out with CRLF
# endings, and `npm run format:check` then fails on a clean clone for every file in the repo —
# while the same check passes in CI on Linux. Pinning the working tree to LF on every platform
# is what makes the CI gate reproducible locally.
#
# Git already stores these blobs with LF, so this changes what is checked out, not what is committed.
* text=auto eol=lf
